From the Pythagorean Theorem,
\[\cos \frac{\theta}{2} = \sqrt{1 - \sin^2 \frac{\theta}{2}} = \sqrt{1 - \frac{x - 1}{2x}} = \sqrt{\frac{x + 1}{2x}}.\]Then
\[\tan \frac{\theta}{2} = \frac{\sin \frac{\theta}{2}}{\cos \frac{\theta}{2}} = \sqrt{\frac{x - 1}{x + 1}}.\]Then
\begin{align*}
\tan \theta &= \frac{2 \tan \frac{\theta}{2}}{1 - \tan^2 \frac{\theta}{2}} \\
&= \frac{2 \sqrt{\frac{x - 1}{x + 1}}}{1 - \frac{x - 1}{x + 1}} \\
&= \frac{2 \sqrt{(x - 1)(x + 1)}}{2} \\
&= \sqrt{x^2 - 1}.
\end{align*}
The answer is \sqrt{x^2 - 1}

